- Added ETag support to the osquery config endpoint (`/api/osquery/config`): agents that send an `If-None-Match` validator now receive `304 Not Modified` when their configuration is unchanged, reducing agent config bandwidth.
- Added an `osquery.redis_config_etags` server option (`FLEET_OSQUERY_REDIS_CONFIG_ETAGS`, default on): config check-ins with a matching validator are answered `304 Not Modified` directly from a Redis-backed ETag store, skipping the config build and its database reads entirely. The short circuit fails open (any Redis error falls back to a full build) and is bypassed automatically for deployments with 2017 packs or label-scoped reports.
- Added ETag support to `osquery-perf` simulated hosts, including stats for conditional config requests and estimated bandwidth saved, for load-testing the above.
